  fruitCountRange: {x: 0, y: 0}
  icon: {fileID: 21300000, guid: f1d0e334fffd26a4198d074ad071c680, type: 3}
  summary: A vining fruit (yes, botanically a fruit!) that keeps flowering and ripening
    new tomatoes for weeks after the first pick.
  facts:
  - Tomatoes start green and turn red as they ripen, when the plant breaks down chlorophyll
    and builds up a red pigment called lycopene.
  - One healthy tomato plant can keep producing fruit for two to three months if
    you keep picking the ripe ones.
  - Picking ripe tomatoes regularly encourages the plant to set more fruit.
  - Tomatoes are related to potatoes and peppers -- they're all in the nightshade
    family.
